# No manual version bumps

Release versions are derived from git tags and the PR template Major/Minor/Patch
checkboxes by `.github/workflows/release.yml` (`@dg/cli` `version:bump` and
`version:release-info`) and injected at build time via `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_VERSION`
in `apps/web/next.config.ts`. The Release workflow never pushes version-bump
commits onto PR branches, so open PRs never conflict on `package.json`.

Agents and humans must never change the `version` field in the root
`package.json`.

## Hard ban

- NEVER edit the `version` field in the root `package.json`
- NEVER run `npm version`, `pnpm version`, or any local release bump for this repo
- NEVER include a version change in a feature/fix/chore commit
- NEVER "helpfully" bump the version to match a release, tag, or bot commit
- NEVER stage or commit a `package.json` diff whose only (or partial) change is
  `version`

## Allowed

- Leave `version` untouched in every commit
- Check Major/Minor/Patch in the PR template so `.github/workflows/release.yml`
  computes the release version and tags the squash merge commit on `main`
- Run `turbo drop-bot-commits` on older branches that still carry a legacy
  `github-actions[bot]` `Bump version to v...` commit

## If you already changed it

Revert only the `version` field to whatever it was on `origin/main`. Do not
invent a new semver.
